{
  "abstract": "Formalization of Basic Functional Categories, Functional Categories, the pointfree CoEndoYoneda Isomorphism Theorem, and its equivalence with computational purity (monad idempotency) for Kleisli categories. Given a category C and a functional functor FF : Type u ⥤ C, we define the CoYoneda endofunctor CYEF(Z) = CYF(Z) ⋙ FF, the global-like endofunctor G = CYEF(FF(T)), and prove the CoEndoYoneda isomorphism (CYEF(Z) ⟶ (EF ⋙ G)) ≃ (FF(T) ⟶ G(EF(Z))). We prove that evaluating the forward isomorphism on id_G recovers the terminal unit component η.app(FF(T)), verify that Type u with the identity functor is a canonical Functional Category, and prove that for the Kleisli category KleisliCat M of a lawful monad M with canonical identity-on-objects functor KFF, BasicFunctionalCategory (KleisliCat M) (KFF M) holds if and only if M is an idempotent (pure) monad. Finally, we derive the terminal subsingleton theorem (IsPure M → Subsingleton (M T)) and classify seven standard computational effects (Option, List, Read, Write, State, Cont, and ErrorState/IO).",
